{"name":"Ghost Town","hex":"#beb6a8","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ghost town","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A town which has become deserted, usually due to failing economic activity, especially one that still has substantial visible remains.","Anything that has been deserted or abandoned, or has been empty all along."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ghost_town"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ghost town","blocks":[{"text":"A ghost town is an abandoned or largely depopulated human settlement that usually contains substantial, visible remaining buildings and infrastructure, such as roads. A town often becomes a ghost town because the economic activity that supported it has failed or ended for any reason. The town may also have declined because of natural or human-caused disasters such as floods, prolonged droughts, government actions, war, pollution, or nuclear and radiation-related accidents and incidents. The term can sometimes refer to cities, towns, and neighbourhoods that, though still populated, are significantly less so than in past years; for example, those affected by high levels of unemployment and dereliction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Village_martyr_d%27Oradour-sur-Glane_10.jpg/330px-Village_martyr_d%27Oradour-sur-Glane_10.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ghost_town","wikidata":"Q74047"},{"title":"Ghost Town (1936 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Ghost Town is a 1936 American Western film directed by Harry L. Fraser and starring Harry Carey, David Sharpe and Ruth Findlay. It was produced by William Berke"}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/41/Ghost_Town_%281936_film%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ghost_Town_(1936_film)","wikidata":"Q55612625"},{"title":"Ghost","blocks":[{"text":"In folklore, a ghost is the soul or spirit of a dead person or non-human animal that is believed by some people to be able to appear to the living. In ghostlore, descriptions of ghosts vary widely, from an invisible presence to translucent or barely visible wispy shapes to realistic, lifelike forms, whether they resemble humans or animals. The deliberate attempt to contact the spirit of a deceased person is known as necromancy, or in spiritism as a séance. Other terms associated with it are apparition, haunt, haint, phantom, poltergeist, shade, specter, spirit, spook, wraith, demon, and ghoul."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/0/02/Hammersmith_Ghost.PNG/330px-Hammersmith_Ghost.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ghost","wikidata":"Q45529"},{"title":"Town","blocks":[{"text":"A town is a type of a human settlement, generally larger than a village but smaller than a city."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Clear_sky_afternoon_on_the_Ipswich_Waterfront.jpg/330px-Clear_sky_afternoon_on_the_Ipswich_Waterfront.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Town","wikidata":"Q3957"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Aghdam_6.jpg/500px-Aghdam_6.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Aghdam_6.jpg/1280px-Aghdam_6.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Aghdam_6.jpg/500px-Aghdam_6.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Nature slowly reclaiming the ruins in Aghdam (2010)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAghdam_6.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/An_aerial_view_showing_destruction_in_Rafah_after_Israeli_forces_withdrawal_and_as_the_ceasefire_took_hold%2C_Gaza_Strip.jpg/500px-An_aerial_view_showing_destruction_in_Rafah_after_Israeli_forces_withdrawal_and_as_the_ceasefire_took_hold%2C_Gaza_Strip.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/An_aerial_view_showing_destruction_in_Rafah_after_Israeli_forces_withdrawal_and_as_the_ceasefire_took_hold%2C_Gaza_Strip.jpg/500px-An_aerial_view_showing_destruction_in_Rafah_after_Israeli_forces_withdrawal_and_as_the_ceasefire_took_hold%2C_Gaza_Strip.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Rafah, destroyed (2025)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAn_aerial_view_showing_destruction_in_Rafah_after_Israeli_forces_withdrawal_and_as_the_ceasefire_took_hold%2C_Gaza_Strip.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Abandoned_farmhouse%2C_overgrown.jpg/500px-Abandoned_farmhouse%2C_overgrown.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Abandoned_farmhouse%2C_overgrown.jpg/1280px-Abandoned_farmhouse%2C_overgrown.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Abandoned_farmhouse%2C_overgrown.jpg/500px-Abandoned_farmhouse%2C_overgrown.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"As farms industrialise, smaller farms are no longer economically viable, leading to rural decay.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAbandoned_farmhouse%2C_overgrown.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Famagusta-Varosha_2007.JPG/500px-Famagusta-Varosha_2007.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Famagusta-Varosha_2007.JPG/1280px-Famagusta-Varosha_2007.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Famagusta-Varosha_2007.JPG/500px-Famagusta-Varosha_2007.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Prior to the Turkish invasion of Cyprus in 1974, Varosha, now falling into ruin, was a modern tourist area.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFamagusta-Varosha_2007.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Akarmaraghosttown.jpg/500px-Akarmaraghosttown.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Akarmaraghosttown.jpg/500px-Akarmaraghosttown.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Akarmara, a mining town in Abkhazia/Georgia, was abandoned in the early 1990s due to the War in Abkhazia.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAkarmaraghosttown.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Motserrat_damage.jpg/500px-Motserrat_damage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Motserrat_damage.jpg/1280px-Motserrat_damage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Motserrat_damage.jpg/500px-Motserrat_damage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Plymouth, Montserrat is the only ghost town that is the capital of a modern political territory. It was rendered uninhabitable and evacuated in 1995 after being inundated with volcanic ash from the eruption of the Soufrière Hills Volcano.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMotserrat_damage.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Craco_il_paese_fantasma.jpg/500px-Craco_il_paese_fantasma.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Craco_il_paese_fantasma.jpg/1280px-Craco_il_paese_fantasma.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Craco_il_paese_fantasma.jpg/500px-Craco_il_paese_fantasma.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Craco, Italy, was abandoned due to a landslide in 1963. It has since become a popular film set.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACraco_il_paese_fantasma.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Pripyat-today.jpg/500px-Pripyat-today.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Pripyat-today.jpg/500px-Pripyat-today.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pripyat, Ukraine, was abandoned after the Chernobyl disaster.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APripyat-today.jpg"}],"sounds":{"ghost town":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/19/En-au-ghost_town.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/1/19/En-au-ghost_town.ogg/En-au-ghost_town.ogg.mp3"}]}}}